Report: src/henchman/agents/working_memory.py\n## Date: 2025-03-16T10:00:00Z\n##
Bug Summary\nThe `_validate_lines_read` method in `WorkingMemoryEntry` 
incorrectly accepts invalid strings like `"full,invalid"` because it only checks
if `"full"` is present, ignoring other invalid content. This violates the 
principle that validation should reject invalid input.\n\n## Lens\n**Phase 1: 
The Intent vs. Reality Check** - Logic gap where invalid input is silently 
accepted due to overly permissive validation.\n\n## Expected vs. Observed\n| 
